  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nBoth near and long range deterministic/ensemble models remain\nstaunch in a fairly persistent forecast featuring surface high\npressure and varying upper ridging dominating the weather\npattern through at least this coming weekend. The result favors\nnear to above normal temperature, dry weather, light wind, and a\npreponderance of sunshine. This is likely to result in large\ndiurnal temperature ranges, with chances for patchy morning \nfrost (generally where the growing season has ended). Those with\nfall plants like mums should remain aware of this threat. \n\nThe only subtle flow change is a mostly weak shortwave that \ndrops over the region overnight Wednesday into Thursday,\npotentially offering a few more clouds and less than 20%\nprobabilities for squeezing out some light rain in areas close \nto Lake Erie.",
